# Feature branches

`pablos-ideas` is the side branch that holds every coded idea. Each functionality lives on its own branch from `main`, so it can become its own pull request.

When starting a functionality:

1. Create the branch from `main`, not from `pablos-ideas` or another feature branch.
2. Commit only that functionality on the new branch.
3. Merge that branch into `pablos-ideas`. Keep the feature branch.

```powershell
git fetch upstream
git switch main
git merge --ff-only upstream/main
git switch -c mixer-redesign
# commit only this functionality
git push -u origin mixer-redesign
git switch pablos-ideas
git merge mixer-redesign
```

`upstream` is `musescore/MuseScore`. `origin` is the `pabdelhay/MuseScore` fork. Pull requests go from one feature branch to `upstream` `main`.

Current branches:

- `chord-symbol-picker` — chord picker
- `mixer-redesign` — mixer chords section
- `pablos-ideas` — both, plus later functionalities after each is merged

Do not add a second functionality to an existing feature branch. Do not open a pull request from `pablos-ideas`. `cursor-rules` is not a feature branch.

`.cursor/` is stored on the fork-only branch `cursor-rules`. Fetch it and publish edits with the cursor-rules branch rule. `IDEAS.md` and logs stay untracked. These paths are listed in `.git/info/exclude`, not in `.gitignore`, so a feature-branch commit never includes them. Before pushing, the branch diff should contain only that functionality. Do not include the `muse` submodule pointer unless the change is about that submodule.
